{
  "title": "Intramembranous Bone Formation",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9007/intramembranous-bone-formation",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 15 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "One of the two essential processes during",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**development formation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**fracture healing**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "also commonly known as contact healing, and Haversian remodeling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occurs **without a cartilage model** (unlike enchondral ossification)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Examples of intramembranous ossification",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**embryonic flat bone** formation (skull, maxilla, mandible, pelvis, clavicle, subperiosteal surface of long bone)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**distraction osteogenesis** bone formation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**blastem bone** (occurs in children with amputations)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**fracture healing with rigid fixation** (compression plate)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "one component of healing with intramedullary nailing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "conditions with defects in intramembranous ossification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**cleidocranial dysplasia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "caused by defect in intramembranous ossification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "caused by mutation in **CBFA1** (also know as Runx2) located on chromosome 6",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanism",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Steps of intramembranous bone formation aggregation of undifferentiated mesenchymal cells osteoblast differentiation organic matrix deposition",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Regulation and signaling",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "controlled by pathway called canonical Wnt and Hedgehog signaling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "beta-catenin enters cells and induces cells to form osteoblasts which then proceed with intramembranous bone formation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "important transcription factors include **CBFA1** (also know as Runx2) and **osterix (OSX)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**sclerostin, created by the SOST gene, decreases bone mass by inhibiting the Wnt pathway**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
